<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37632" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-gĕro</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>, gestum, 3,
				v. a.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To bear</i> or <i>carry before</i>
			(post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">speculum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 4, p. 157, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To do before;</i> only <i>subst.</i>:
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praegesta</span></b> ,
				ōrum, n., <i>things done before</i>, <i>former things</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oblivio praegestorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
					Aur. Tard. 1, 5</span></i>
			, n. 150.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
